{"_id":"68a736358ec3d8323af1db37","nodeId":"FHZSxSiOZYNBEz6tu8wuF","roadmapSlug":"rust","createdAt":"2025-08-21T15:07:32.844Z","description":"# Integers\n\nIn Rust, integers are a primitive data type that hold whole number values, both positive and negative. Integer types in Rust can be divided into signed and unsigned ones:\n\n*   Signed integers, denoted by \"i\", are those that can hold negative, zero, and positive values.\n*   Unsigned integers, denoted by \"u\", only hold zero and positive values.","resources":[{"type":"official","title":"Integer Data Type in Rust","url":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/book/ch03-02-data-types.html#integer-types","_id":"6a7f4b36cb44947debcfddb0"},{"type":"official","title":"Machine-dependent Integer Types","url":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/reference/types/numeric.html#machine-dependent-integer-types","_id":"6a7f4b36cb44947debcfddb1"},{"type":"article","title":"Rust Data Types (With Examples)","url":"https://www.programiz.com/rust/data-types#integer-type","_id":"6a7f4b36cb44947debcfddb2"},{"type":"article","title":"Integer Types","url":"https://rust-book.cs.brown.edu/ch03-02-data-types.html#integer-types","_id":"6a7f4b36cb44947debcfddb3"}],"updatedAt":"2026-08-14T17:07:02.070Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/rust/content/FHZSxSiOZYNBEz6tu8wuF.md"}